{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1273652-so-i-was-reincarnated-as-a-slime-kith","id":1273652,"title":"So I was reincarnated as a Slime Kith...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-09T20:21:29-08:00","id":1273652,"title":"So I was reincarnated as a Slime Kith...","content":"Between a certain anime showing this season and some jokes about how parts of my changeling game are &quot;monstergirls doing monstergirl things&quot; I've been thinking about a Slime kith. So I've had a couple ideas on how to best do this and wanted some advice on which way to go..<br /> <br /> <br /> Make them a Denizen Race! This gets around the human shape problem! lets them pop in and out of reality as needed that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Second Idea: have them function like Pooka with a Slime for and a humanoid form(I did say Slime tensai was inspiring this)<br /> <br /> <br /> I am not sure which would work better or if there's maybe an even better idea out there..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T03:12:40-08:00","id":1273695,"title":"","content":"I never created a Denizen group, but when I am thinking about a new kith, I usually ask first: What dreams/nightmares do I think would make this kith?<br /> <br /> Helps to give a direction to the birthrights, relations, variations, etc...<br /> <br /> A Slime Kith, I dont know. Maybe the fear of slime disgusting things, like mold? Wouldnt be a very &quot;friendly monster girl&quot; kind of kith on this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T12:18:51-08:00","id":1273766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1273652-so-i-was-reincarnated-as-a-slime-kith?p=1273695#post1273695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never created a Denizen group, but when I am thinking about a new kith, I usually ask first: What dreams/nightmares do I think would make this kith?<br /> <br /> Helps to give a direction to the birthrights, relations, variations, etc...<br /> <br /> A Slime Kith, I dont know. Maybe the fear of slime disgusting things, like mold? Wouldnt be a very &quot;friendly monster girl&quot; kind of kith on this case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wolptingers show that kiths can be relatively modern in birth. Some are primal dreams and those are what i'd consider the big kiths but then there are smaller groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T12:29:43-08:00","id":1273770,"title":"","content":"So, let's do some brainstorming.<br /> <br /> Slimes would be modern - very modern, more so than even the Wolpertinger, since they first really gain definition as a critter with the Dragon Quest video games.<br /> <br /> Given their point of origin, their greatest concentration would be in Japan and its associated Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Running off Manbat, what associations do Slimes have? Mooks. Mutability. Amorphousness. Fluidity. Absorption.<br /> <br /> Hm. Not sure that's enough of a desire/fear for one of the major Kithain, at least to me, but it does seem rather elemental. That would point to slime Inanimae, but there aren't really any Slime Anchors in the physical world.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I'd eye a Slime kith as Gallain - too new to participate in the War of the Trees and so truly be Denizens, don't really have the material basis to be Inanimae, and don't really embody enough of an aspiration/fear for the major Kithain.<br /> <br /> Alright, then. Gallain it is. But how do they manifest in the material world?<br /> <br /> Honestly, my mental model of a Slime kith would have them closer to the Denizens than anything else; they come at humanity from an outside perspective, rather than having been born and raised human. So they possess a human, or they manifest a physical form, and go about exploring the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> As a kith, I'd see them as essentially being new to everything, curious and eager to learn about everything they can.<br /> <br /> Dunno if any of that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T12:38:22-08:00","id":1273772,"title":"","content":"I have Dragon Half going through my head, wherein slimes who choose to live among humans must concentrate in stressful moments (canon examples include being hit by comical falling rocks and childbirth) or else lose their human form for a short while, reverting to slime form. While in human form they can marry humans and interbreed with them, though any children are slimes.<br /> <br /> So I would say that their weakness is the risk of spontaneously shapeshifting, while their strengths ought to be natural damage resistance in all forms, and either a charisma bonus in human form to reflect the magical nature of their human form, or some kind of acid attack in slime form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T17:37:49-08:00","id":1273812,"title":"","content":"Personally I\u2019d look for Fantasy Friends for inspiration as it has slimes as playable race that can hide amongst humans, with variable results. Going from there I\u2019d say that having either the ability to squeeze themselves through anywhere a liquid could, but since that is stepping on Sluagh toes, or the ability to change their size from diminutive to large, it would still let them fit through small space but seperate them from the Sluagh. Or for something more unpresidented in Changeling giving them Two of Me birthright that allows them to temporarily split themselves into two slimes later melding back into one. Shapeshifting could also be high on my list of options with the caveat that despite their form they are always made of slime.<br /> <br /> Other possible slimish things would be absoption of items into ones body or gaining grappling bonuses from taking parts of your opponent into your slime body and trapping them in.<br /> <br /> As for the Frailty anything from being creepy, and gaining social penalties, since you are a slime pretending to be human, to being unable to speak only able to produce odd cooing or bubbling noices to communicate, this mostly if you want to inject your slimes with a dose of humour linked into how cute they are in dragon quest series. Or to emphazise their slime nature perhaps they are despite any human shell or other disguise always slightly moist and gooy to touch, giving social penalties and making them easier to track as they tend to leave a trail of goo.<br /> <br /> Just throwing ideas without too much thought so YMMV on these but perhaps they can act as inspiration. Perhaps I\u2019ll return to this with actually thought out mechanics but that depends on my free time and general amount of insomnia.<br /> <br /> I would either make them a Kith or a Denizen myself, in the former case slimes would have a generally fluid humanoid form and in the latter they likely resembled Dragon Quest slimes. <br /> <br /> If I made them into a Kith I\u2019d likely make a Thallain version of them as well as the dreaded Gelatinious Cube that would have acidic absorption as one of their Endowements and perhaps their acidic nature, either social penalties for being spiteful and acidic or literally acidic nature as in they leave acid stains where they touch and slowly absorb and dissolve their own clothing and carried items, as their Vulnerability with their second Endovement being similar to whatever shapechanging I\u2019d end up giving the normal slimes, size change, fluid form or shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Also should a Slime ever gain Title background he would manifest a small crown on him and grow slightly bigger, how big depends on the Title backgrounds level naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T18:15:16-08:00","id":1274119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1273652-so-i-was-reincarnated-as-a-slime-kith#post1273652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between a certain anime showing this season and some jokes about how parts of my changeling game are &quot;monstergirls doing monstergirl things&quot; I've been thinking about a Slime kith. So I've had a couple ideas on how to best do this and wanted some advice on which way to go..<br /> <br /> <br /> Make them a Denizen Race! This gets around the human shape problem! lets them pop in and out of reality as needed that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Second Idea: have them function like Pooka with a Slime for and a humanoid form(I did say Slime tensai was inspiring this)<br /> <br /> <br /> I am not sure which would work better or if there's maybe an even better idea out there..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What exactly are &quot;monster girl things?&quot;<br /> <br /> The only stuff that comes to mind is forming a protagonist's harem.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I would go with the idea of them having a humanoid shape, since I've seen a few slimes that allow them to have a humanoid shape.<br /> <br /> As a Kith, they could have an ability enabling them to become hyper malleable by expending glamour. Though the hard part would be finding a way to translate that into the Autumn World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T20:42:27-08:00","id":1274131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1273652-so-i-was-reincarnated-as-a-slime-kith?p=1274119#post1274119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What exactly are &quot;monster girl things?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Among my friends we call a lot of slice of life anime &quot;Cute girls doing cute girl things&quot; but there's a sort of similar setup of supernatural being just sort of.. having slice of life stuff. Which we've taken to calling &quot;Monster girls doing monster girl things&quot;<br /> <br /> Basicially its changeling run as a slice of life. Focusing on say how hard it is to be a Centaur pooka, or being a cute harpy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T08:33:28-08:00","id":1282856,"title":"","content":"Hmm, considering Slimes are often depicted as having a malleable or amorphous shape, maybe they could represent dreams of personal identity and transhumanism?<br /> <br /> The slime alters themselves into a whatever appearance they feel comfortable with, but their personality remains the same regardless of what they look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}